s("Look at another person as a soul, as someone loved by God, and your day becomes a feast. Look at him only with the eyes of the flesh, and you begin to sink.", ["portrait", "angel"])
s("We live in two worlds at once: a visible one, and an invisible one.", ["landscape", "angel"], big="two")
s("And many of us sleepwalk through the second.", ["night", "bed"], big="sleepwalk")
s("From the moment we wake until the moment we sleep, a war is being fought, and the prize is the soul.", ["battle", "angel"], big="soul")
s("It sounds dramatic. But look honestly at a single day of your thoughts, your words and your choices, and you can see the ground being lost, inch by inch.", ["battle", "thinker"])
s("Try this. Spend one Sunday without your phone, or at least without the internet.", ["church", "landscape"])
s("Notice how hard it is. The restlessness, the itch, the reaching hand.", ["thinker"], big="restlessness")
s("We cling to the very things that hurt us, and then we are surprised that we feel miserable.", ["despair"])
s("There is something in us that sabotages us and lies to us about it.", ["shadow", "demon"])
s("The old word for it is diabolical. It comes from the Greek diaballein: to throw across, to split apart, to slander.", ["demon", "book"], big="diabolical")
s("Its opposite is the symbolic: that which throws together, and makes whole.", ["light", "church"], big="symbolic")
s("In Paradise Lost, John Milton puts it this way: the mind is its own place, and in itself can make a heaven of hell, a hell of heaven.", ["milton", "hell"], big="heaven", gap=1.5)
s("A disciplined mind can find peace in a prison. A restless one can turn a palace into a torment.", ["prison", "palace"])
