s("So not every thought in your head is yours.", ["thinker", "shadow"], big="yours")
s("Every act of self-hatred, every curse on your own body, is a small agreement with the accuser.", ["mirror", "despair"], big="agreement")
s("Renounce it. Say instead: I do not hate myself. I forgive myself.", ["light", "prayer"])
s("When the inner voice says nobody cares for you, or that God could never forgive what you have done, you are in the battle.", ["despair", "night"])
s("Consent to it, and it becomes a contract. The darkness has no strength of its own. We lend it ours.", ["demon", "hell"], big="contract")
s("In his life of Saint Anthony, Athanasius tells how the devil tried every thought on the young monk, and every disguise.", ["anthony", "desert"], big="Anthony")
s("At last the spirit of lust appeared to him as a small dark boy, boasting of all the men it had brought down.", ["anthony", "demon"])
s("Anthony called it weak as a child, and sang a psalm: the Lord is my helper, and I shall look down on my enemies.", ["anthony", "prayer"])
s("And the spirit fled, and did not come near him again.", ["anthony", "desert"], gap=1.3)
s("Ignorance of scripture, Saint Jerome wrote, is ignorance of Christ.", ["jerome", "book"], big="ignorance")
s("Evagrius adds one thing: answer the thought quickly, before it settles in.", ["sword", "monk"], big="quickly")
s("He borrowed the idea from the Stoics, who spoke of first movements.", ["stoic", "statue"])
s("A flash of anger at an injustice is a first movement. It is not yet a sin. What matters is what you do next.", ["anger", "thinker"])
s("Assent to it, feed it, and the first movement becomes a passion, and the passion becomes a deed.", ["fire"], big="passion")
s("The Stoic sage sorted his impressions, true from false. The monk sorts his thoughts, clean from unclean. The old name for this is discernment.", ["stoic", "monk"], big="discernment")
s("Saint Ignatius of Loyola later taught it as a craft: to notice which movements of the soul draw us toward God, and which draw us away.", ["ignatius", "prayer"])
s("Evagrius aimed even higher: not only to avoid sinful deeds, but to grow free of the very thoughts that lead to them.", ["monk", "light"])
s("A thought we dwell on leaves an image behind in the memory, like a stain on glass, and it clouds the mind.", ["window", "fog"], big="stain")
s("No evil thought, Evagrius insisted, comes from our nature. The seed the Lord sowed in his field was good.", ["field", "harvest"], big="good", gap=1.5)

